            <ArticleTitle>[Ischemic heart disease and the biological age of men over 40].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>22-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A population of 40- to 64-year-old males (normal subjects and coronary patients) were examined in order to estimate their biological age on the basis of cardiovascular and respiratory functional parameters and multiple regression analysis dynamometry in relation to hormonal status; it may be considered as a factor, contributing to cardiovascular pathology.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
